WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.600
Define the feature contract: graph or mesh, node order, units,
field channels and normalisation. Use a compatible model to propose damage.

00:06.600 --> 00:09.800
Check admissibility, including bounds and irreversibility,
and the declared residual or constraint tolerance.

00:09.800 --> 00:12.400
A passing proposal may be accepted as the checked state.

00:12.400 --> 00:17.600
A failing proposal requires reference correction.
The corrected field must then be checked again.

00:17.600 --> 00:19.800
Accept the corrected field when the second check passes.

00:19.800 --> 00:22.700
If the second check fails, stop and report nonconvergence.
Acceptance requires a passing check.

00:22.700 --> 00:26.500
Measure the complete route: prediction, conversion, checking and correction.
Compare total runtime alongside field quality and failure rates.
